            <ArticleTitle>Radiology-pathology conference: primary adrenal lymphoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>156-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.clinimag.2011.08.022</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of a 62-year-old man with a history of type II diabetes mellitus who presented to our emergency department with back pain and right upper quadrant abdominal pain associated with vomiting and weight loss. A computed tomographic scan of the abdomen and pelvis demonstrated a large adrenal mass, and subsequent biopsy showed primary adrenal lymphoma.</AbstractText>
